From 7ace024dfddb0dbeed47bb9ac9f0a2a5fc20f177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 17:58:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(deepseek-v41): stage Engram rows from disk

Upstream base: d05da62e9ccdf8e342b15bf6785d83224cc165af plus carries
through 8a82c50a6a3147ed14adb15a90bc7cb4322c0829.
Rationale: the two immutable Engram tables are about 189 GiB globally and cannot
remain resident while preserving useful KV capacity on three 128 GiB Sparks.
Quality: hashes and FP8/E8M0 checkpoint rows are unchanged; only requested rows
are staged through B12X before the upstream Engram computation.
Tests: ruff, format, py_compile, exact filter/range unit tests, and config gates;
deterministic output, I/O, TTFT, and concurrency qualification remain required.
Upstream status: local carry intended for coordinated vLLM/B12X contribution.

